  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Srinivasan (Petitioner)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Srinivasan (Petitioner), petitioner argues that, despite his convictions, he is not categorically ineligible for discretionary relief from removal."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, is there a mootness problem because the petitioner re\u2011entered the country illegally and committed another minor crime?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Saharsky",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 32,
              "start": 32
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Saharsky, does the State offense correspond to an offense under the Controlled Substances Act (CSA) and thus to a Federal offense?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 35,
              "start": 35
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, in Lopez, did the petitioner prevail because the conduct would not have been a felony under Federal law?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, suppose we are dealing with the Armed Career Criminal Act\u2014how does that affect the analysis?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, is the repeated conduct (recidivism) essential to the argument under the Federal statute?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts: We will hear argument first this morning in Case 09\u201160, Carachuri\u2011Rosendo v. Holder. Mr. Srinivasan."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer: I don't know. It seems to me you go further than you need to and, moreover, imagine a State offense that just says possession of marijuana, zero to 5 years."
      }
    ],
